    {
        "title" : "t-SNE + K-Means: Data visualization and Clustering",
        "date_published" : "2025-09-12T23:53:24+08:00",
        "date_modified" : "2025-09-12T23:53:24+08:00",
        "id" : "https://martinlwx.github.io/en/k-means-tutorial/",
        "url" : "https://martinlwx.github.io/en/k-means-tutorial/",
        "summary": " K-Means AlgorithmI recently used the K-Means algorithm for clustering in my work. While reviewing my notes on the topic, I decided to publish them online :)\nK-Means is a clustering algorithm that assigns each sample to one of the $K$ clusters.\nHow does AK-Means algorithm work? Data PreparationK-Means algorithm relies on distance calculations, so data should be normalized to prevent features with larger scales from dominating the results. The normalization can be achieved by the Scikit-Learn library as follows.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "MartinLwx"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch2 id=\"k-means-algorithm\" class=\"headerLink\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"#k-means-algorithm\" class=\"header-mark\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eK-Means Algorithm\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eI recently used the K-Means algorithm for clustering in my work. While reviewing my notes on the topic, I decided to publish them online :)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eK-Means is a clustering algorithm that assigns each sample to one of the $K$ clusters.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 id=\"how-does-ak-means-algorithm-work\" class=\"headerLink\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"#how-does-ak-means-algorithm-work\" class=\"header-mark\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eHow does AK-Means algorithm work?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"data-preparation\" class=\"headerLink\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"#data-preparation\" class=\"header-mark\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eData Preparation\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eK-Means algorithm relies on distance calculations, so data should be normalized to prevent features with larger scales from dominating the results. The normalization can be achieved by the \u003ccode\u003eScikit-Learn\u003c/code\u003e library as follows.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight is-open show-line-numbers  tw:group tw:my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv class=\"\n    \n    tw:flex \n    tw:flex-row\n    tw:flex-1 \n    tw:justify-between \n    tw:w-full tw:bg-bgColor-secondary\n    \"\u003e      \n    \u003cbutton \n      class=\"\n        code-block-button\n        tw:mx-2 \n        tw:flex\n        tw:flex-row\n        tw:flex-1\"\n      aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\n          \u003cspan class=\"tw:group-[.is-open]:rotate-90 tw:transition-[transform] tw:duration-500 tw:ease-in-out tw:print:hidden! tw:w-min tw:h-min tw:my-1 tw:mx-1\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"icon\"\n    xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 512\"\u003e\u003c!-- Font Awesome Free 5.15.4 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license/free (Icons: CC BY 4.0, Fon