ont Awesome Free 5.15.4 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license/free (Icons: CC BY 4.0, Fonts: SIL OFL 1.1, Code: MIT License) --\u003e\u003cpath d=\"M173.898 439.404l-166.4-166.4c-9.997-9.997-9.997-26.206 0-36.204l36.203-36.204c9.997-9.998 26.207-9.998 36.204 0L192 312.69 432.095 72.596c9.997-9.997 26.207-9.997 36.204 0l36.203 36.204c9.997 9.997 9.997 26.206 0 36.204l-294.4 294.401c-9.998 9.997-26.207 9.997-36.204-.001z\"/\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003c/button\u003e\n        \n      \u003cbutton \n        class=\"\n          tw:select-none \n          tw:mx-2 \n          tw:block \n          tw:group-[.is-open]:hidden \n          tw:print:hidden!\" \n        disabled\n        aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"icon\"\n    xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\"\u003e\u003c!-- Font Awesome Free 5.15.4 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license/free (Icons: CC BY 4.0, Fonts: SIL OFL 1.1, Code: MIT License) --\u003e\u003cpath d=\"M328 256c0 39.8-32.2 72-72 72s-72-32.2-72-72 32.2-72 72-72 72 32.2 72 72zm104-72c-39.8 0-72 32.2-72 72s32.2 72 72 72 72-32.2 72-72-32.2-72-72-72zm-352 0c-39.8 0-72 32.2-72 72s32.2 72 72 72 72-32.2 72-72-32.2-72-72-72z\"/\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/button\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"tw:block tw:m-0 tw:p-0\"\u003e\u003ccode \n    id=\"codeblock-id-30\" \n    class=\"\n      chroma \n      tw:block! \n      tw:p-0\n      tw:m-0\n      tw:transition-[max-height] \n      tw:duration-500 \n      tw:ease-in-out \n      tw:group-[.is-closed]:max-h-0! \n      tw:group-[.is-wrap]:text-wrap\n      tw:overflow-y-hidden\n      tw:overflow-x-auto\n      tw:scrollbar-thin\n      \"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etorch\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eeinsum\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;i,i-\u0026gt;\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ev\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ev\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 id=\"wrap-up\" class=\"headerLink\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"#wrap-up\" class=\"header-mark\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWrap-up\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eI like the \u003ccode\u003etorch.einsum\u003c/code\u003e API for its simplicity. It gives me the experience of \u003cem\u003edeclarative programming\u003c/em\u003e, that is, you describe the input and output and it will automatically figure out how to do the calculates. Another benifit is that it\u0026rsquo;s \u003cem\u003eself-documenting\u003c/em\u003e.  :)\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Two different APIs related to Process Pool in Python",
