\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nc\"\u003einteger\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e))\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003e*\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e@int_list\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBesides, the Query supports the \u003ccode\u003e.\u003c/code\u003e mark. The functionality will change \u003cem\u003edepending on the location of \u003ccode\u003e.\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf \u003ccode\u003e.\u003c/code\u003e appears before the first children (denoted by \u003ccode\u003eS2\u003c/code\u003e), then the \u003ccode\u003eS2\u003c/code\u003e \u003cem\u003emust be\u003c/em\u003e the first children of the parent node (denoted by \u003ccode\u003eS1\u003c/code\u003e). If we want to extract all the first elements in all Python lists, we can write\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight is-open show-line-numbers  tw:group tw:my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv class=\"\n    \n    tw:flex \n    tw:flex-row\n    tw:flex-1 \n    tw:justify-between \n    tw:w-full tw:bg-bgColor-secondary\n    \"\u003e      \n    \u003cbutton \n      class=\"\n        code-block-button\n        tw:mx-2 \n        tw:flex\n        tw:flex-row\n        tw:flex-1\"\n      aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\n          \u003cspan class=\"tw:group-[.is-open]:rotate-90 tw:transition-[transform] tw:duration-500 tw:ease-in-out tw:print:hidden! tw:w-min tw:h-min tw:my-1 tw:mx-1\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"icon\"\n    xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 512\"\u003e\u003c!-- Font Awesome Free 5.15.4 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license/free (Icons: CC BY 4.0, Fonts: SIL OFL 1.1, Code: MIT License) --\u003e\u003cpath d=\"M285.476 272.971L91.132 467.314c-9.373 9.373-24.569 9.373-33.94