-36.204c9.997-9.998 26.207-9.998 36.204 0L192 312.69 432.095 72.596c9.997-9.997 26.207-9.997 36.204 0l36.203 36.204c9.997 9.997 9.997 26.206 0 36.204l-294.4 294.401c-9.998 9.997-26.207 9.997-36.204-.001z\"/\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003c/button\u003e\n        \n      \u003cbutton \n        class=\"\n          tw:select-none \n          tw:mx-2 \n          tw:block \n          tw:group-[.is-open]:hidden \n          tw:print:hidden!\" \n        disabled\n        aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"icon\"\n    xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\"\u003e\u003c!-- Font Awesome Free 5.15.4 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license/free (Icons: CC BY 4.0, Fonts: SIL OFL 1.1, Code: MIT License) --\u003e\u003cpath d=\"M328 256c0 39.8-32.2 72-72 72s-72-32.2-72-72 32.2-72 72-72 72 32.2 72 72zm104-72c-39.8 0-72 32.2-72 72s32.2 72 72 72 72-32.2 72-72-32.2-72-72-72zm-352 0c-39.8 0-72 32.2-72 72s32.2 72 72 72 72-32.2 72-72-32.2-72-72-72z\"/\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/button\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"tw:block tw:m-0 tw:p-0\"\u003e\u003ccode \n    id=\"codeblock-id-15\" \n    class=\"\n      chroma \n      tw:block! \n      tw:p-0\n      tw:m-0\n      tw:transition-[max-height] \n      tw:duration-500 \n      tw:ease-in-out \n      tw:group-[.is-closed]:max-h-0! \n      tw:group-[.is-wrap]:text-wrap\n      tw:overflow-y-hidden\n      tw:overflow-x-auto\n      tw:scrollbar-thin\n      \"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eapplication: not a procedure;\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eexpected a procedure that can be applied to arguments\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003egiven: 2\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e🚧 The complete SICP exercise solution is still a work in progress. Please refers to \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/MartinLwx/SICP-Exercise-in-Racket\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Solution of Proj4. Scheme Interpreter of CS61A (2021-Fall)",
        "date_published" : "2023-04-21T10:18:16+08:00",
        "date_modified" : "2023-04-21T10:18:16+08:00",
        "id" : "https://martinlwx.github.io/en/proj4-scheme-interpreter-of-cs61a-of-ucb-fa21/",
        "url" : "https://martinlwx.github.io/en/proj4-scheme-interpreter-of-cs61a-of-ucb-fa21/",
        "summary": " IntroRecently, I am reading a book called Crafting interpreters written by Robert Nystrom. In the original book, a Tree-walker interpreter jlox was implemented in Java. And I am trying to rewrite in Python - pylox. I highly recommend it👍. At this moment, I suddenly remembered that there were a few small issues with the Scheme interpreter for CS61A that I had not resolved after finishing it a year ago, which kept it in an unfinished state. So today I opened the project and intended to run through it from beginning to end and talk about the ideas.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "MartinLwx"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch2 id=\"intro\" class=\"headerLink\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"#intro\" class=\"header-mark\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eIntro\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eRecently, I am reading a book called \u003ca href=\"https://craftinginterpreters.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eCrafting interpreters\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e written by Robert Nystrom. In the original book, a Tree-walker interpreter jlox was implemented in Java. And I am trying to rewrite in Python - \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/MartinLwx/pylox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003epylox\u003c/a\u003e. I highly recommend it👍. At this moment, I suddenly remembered that there were a few small issues with the Scheme interpreter for CS61A that I had not resolved after finishing it a year ago, which kept it in an unfinished state. So today I opened the project and intended to run through it from beginning to end and talk about the ideas.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cp\u003eNote: I only quote \u003cstrong\u003epart\u003c/strong\u003e of the original problem description. To make the post more compact, I also omit the irrelevant code :)\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"part-1-the-evaluator\" class=\"headerLink\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"#part-1-the-evaluator\" class=\"header-mark\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003ePart 1. The Evaluator\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"problem-1\" class=\"headerLink\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"#problem-1\" class=\"header-mark\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eProblem 1\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cp\u003eImplement the \u003ccode\u003edefine\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003elookup\u003c/code\u003e methods of the Frame class\u0026hellip;\u003ccode\u003ebindings\u003c/code\u003e is a dictionary representing the bindings in the frame\u0026hellip;\u003ccode\u003eparent\u003c/code\u003e is the parent Frame instance\u0026hellip;The \u003cem\u003eenvironment\u003c/em\u003e for a \u003ccode\u003eFrame\u003c/code\u003e instance consists of that frame, its parent frame, and all its ancestor frames, including the Global Frame.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eProblem 1 is trivial in my opinion. To implement the \u003ccode\u003edefine\u003c/code\u003e function, you just need to save the \u003ccode\u003e{ symbol: value }\u003c/code\u003e in \u003ccode\u003eself.bindings\u003c/code\u003e. As for the \u003ccode\u003elookup\u003c/code\u003e function, we can write a iterative solution or recursive one. The iterative solution is more intuitive though.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight is-open show-line-numbers  tw:group tw:my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv class=\"\n    \n    tw:flex \n    tw:flex-row\n    tw:flex-1 \n    tw:justify-between \n    tw:w-full tw:bg-bgColor-secondary\n    \"\u003e      \n    \u003cbutton \n      class=\"\n        code-block-button\n        tw:mx-2 \n        tw:flex\n        tw:flex-row\n        tw:flex-1\"\n      aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\n          \u003cspan class=\"tw:group-[.is-open]:rotate-90 tw:transition-[transform] tw:duration-500 tw:ease-in-out tw:print:hidden! tw:w-min tw:h-min tw:my-1 tw:mx-1\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"icon\"\n    xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 512\"\u003e\u003c!-- Font Awesome Free 5.15.4 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license/free (Icons: CC BY 4.0, Fonts: SIL OFL 1.1, Code: MIT License) --\u003e\u003cpath d=\"M285.476 272.971L91.132 467.314c-9.373 9.373-24.569 9.373-33.941 0l-22.667-22.667c-9.357-9.357-9.375-24.522-.04-33.901L188.505 256 34.484 101.255c-9.335-9.379-9.317-24.544.04-33.901l22.667-22.667c9.373-9.373 24.569-9.373 33.941 0L285.475 239.03c9.373 9.372 9.373 24.568.001 33.941z\"/\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n          \u003cspan class=\"tw:select-none tw:my-1! tw:block\"\u003epython\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003c/button\u003e\n\n   \u003cdiv class=\"tw:flex\"\u003e\n      \u0