    class=\"\n      chroma \n      tw:block! \n      tw:p-0\n      tw:m-0\n      tw:transition-[max-height] \n      tw:duration-500 \n      tw:ease-in-out \n      tw:group-[.is-closed]:max-h-0! \n      tw:group-[.is-wrap]:text-wrap\n      tw:overflow-y-hidden\n      tw:overflow-x-auto\n      tw:scrollbar-thin\n      \"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ex\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e1.23456\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sa\"\u003ef\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"si\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ex\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"si\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e.3f\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"si\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode\u003e'1.235'\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003ch5 id=\"the--00-issue\" class=\"headerLink\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"#the--00-issue\" class=\"header-mark\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eThe \u003ccode\u003e-0.0\u003c/code\u003e issue\u003c/h5\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe can use \u003ccode\u003ez\u003c/code\u003e to handle negative zero (i.e. \u003ccode\u003e-0.\u003c/code\u003e) since Python3.11. According to the PEP\u003csup id=\"fnref:2\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#fn:2\" class=\"footnote-ref\" role=\"doc-noteref\"\u003e2\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/sup\u003e, programmers usually will suppress negative zero.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight is-open show-line-numbers  tw:group tw:my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv class=\"\n    \n    tw:flex \n    tw:flex-row\n    tw:flex-1 \n    tw:justify-between \n    tw:w-full tw:bg-bgColor-secondary\n    \"\u003e      \n  