03e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"si\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ex\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"si\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003ez.1f\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"si\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# with z, we will get 0.0 rather than -0.0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode\u003e'0.0'\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003ch3 id=\"other-number-representation\" class=\"headerLink\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"#other-number-representation\" class=\"header-mark\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOther number representation\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn Python, we can use the built-in functions to get the representation in other bases including \u003ccode\u003ebin\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eoct\u003c/code\u003e. You may attempt to use \u003ccode\u003e{bin(a)}\u003c/code\u003e to get the binary representation output of \u003ccode\u003ea\u003c/code\u003e. However, the f-strings offers a more elegant way to handle this\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight is-open show-line-numbers  tw:group tw:my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv class=\"\n    \n    tw:flex \n    tw:flex-row\n    tw:flex-1 \n    tw:justify-between \n    tw:w-full tw:bg-bgColor-secondary\n    \"\u003e      \n    \u003cbutton \n      class=\"\n        code-block-button\n        tw:mx-2 \n        tw:flex\n        tw:flex-row\n        tw:flex-1\"\n      aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\n          \u003cspan class=\"tw:group-[.is-open]:rotate-90 tw:transition-[transform] tw:duration-500 tw:ease-in-out tw:print:hidden! tw:w-min tw:h-min tw:my-1 tw:mx-1\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"icon\"\n    xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 512\"\u003e\u003c!-- Font Awesome Free 5.15.4 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - h